A||||12||gomobile||adding a cd changer||||6||
Z||000000||gomobile||09-30-2001||05:29 PM||||I am adding a cd changer BUT I do not want to install ir behind my seats. Has anyone installed it underneathe the passenger seat? As I am thinking of doing it with some minor modifications (height wise). ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-30-2001||05:33 PM||||You'd have to raise the passenger seat considerably, even for the lowest profile CD changers.  This will look odd and you're passenger (trust me, you'll have passengers) will lose alot of headroom.  You'll also have a tough time accessing the door to the changer.  I'd find another place for it.  What about under the passenger side dash?  If you don't mind running some wiring through the front firewall, you could even make a custom enclosure for it in the front trunk.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||09-30-2001||06:01 PM||||I cast my vote for front trunk... You're not losing any active space, like in the trunk or cabin...||||reg||12
Z||000003||tomanyfieros||09-30-2001||06:27 PM||||hang it from the roof, center it with the 3rd brake light.... thats what i iwll be doing.... and i have seen pics of it done.... i cant find them, if i do, i will have someone post them on here for me.... Thanx Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||10-01-2001||02:07 AM||||I bought a combination Kenwood detach face deck with 6 disck CD changer. I left the car at the shop and told them to hang the changer from the airbox above the passenger's feet. Thankfully they screwed up and mounted it to the floor. It's as far forward as you can get before the bulkhead rises up so the passenger didn't loose much legroom. <P>I don't like the location because of:<BR>1) proximity to the heater core<BR>2) even hanging from the airbox the heater core would ruin it when/if it ruptures<BR>3) tall passengers do indeed loose some legroom and tend to rest their feet on it<BR>4) eliminates floormats unless you make the passenger floormat permanently under the changer.<P>I'm gonna remount it in the forward compartment. Is this as good an idea as it sounds? What about heat? rain? dust?<P>Your ideas are appreciated.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierohoho||10-01-2001||03:43 AM||||I would not recomend putting it in the front with the spare without some weatherproof enclosure.<P>On my '84 I noticed on a cold morning that there was a cold draft on my right leg, turns out the plug they put in for non-clutch cars (where the master clutch cylinder goes through the fire wall) had been installed wrong and fallen out.<P>The airflow through that hole at highway speeds was impressive, it was almost like having a vent, so that compartment is not as weatherproof as it appears as I think the wind was coming past the rubber seal.<P>My $0.02<P>Jason, been by the post office yet?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||10-01-2001||07:44 AM||||We have a factory GM cd changer mounted under the hood on the left front fender.  It has been there for over a year and never had a problem.  It is connected to a factory GM late model radio so there is no tell tale sign of the CDs existence to punks looking for stereo equipment to steal.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||RiceCooker||10-01-2001||05:23 PM||||I love mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gul2.jpg">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gul3.jpg">  <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Passengers have never complained and I can reach it at a stop light.<P>It's not hanging from that airbox.<BR>We cut a piece of wood and shaped it so a tab fit in behind the dash. It knid of rested there and we screwed the wood into the front firewall. The piece of wood was spray painted black (so it doesnt look silly) and then we hund the changer from the wood. I have had my heater core go twice and once i got some antifreeze on the changer but nothing significant. It gets kicked a little bit when tall people get in but unless someone purposely boots it....<P>I recommend this to anyonewho wants to spend a few quality hours in the garage.<P>Todd||||reg||6
Z||000008||Mickey_Moose||10-01-2001||05:58 PM||||the best place I seen one of these installed is up on the roof in front of the 3rd brake light - custom box was made and it look like part of the headliner...<P>check it out on this page: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/</A>  <P>(kind of hard to see from the picture, but I does look great in person)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Tim<P>||||reg||10
Z||000009||tomanyfieros||10-01-2001||08:17 PM||||mom told me she sent it, well, searching in the back of here van, i found it laying there.... she lies to me because we dont get along... dad will get it... i will make sure.. Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
